{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFaTL7tLZUWtYBkHW8Fs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] An upgrade leaves files the new version dropped in the installed directory, and nothing reports them\n\nI fixed both review findings in two commits. `npm test` passes: 42 Node tests and both Python suites.\n\n1. **`register(ctx)` test not run by `npm test`** (`2b35572`): the `test` script in `package.json` now also runs `python3 -B test/test_register.py`. To check it, I replaced the `ctx.register_skill(...)` call in `tiiny-router/__init__.py` with `pass`. The old script still exited 0, and the new one exits 1 with 2 failures. With the file restored, it passes. My first attempt to break the file used `sed` with `\\s`, which macOS `sed` doesn't support, so the file was never changed. I caught that and redid the check with a Python edit.\n\n2. **Upgrade leaves dropped files behind** (`f12fafb`): before copying, `install` now deletes any file the previous install's manifest lists but the new version doesn't ship, along with any folders left empty.\n   - It only deletes a file whose hash still matches the manifest. Edited files and files the user added are kept.\n   - It skips any manifest path that points outside the plugin directory.\n   - The new test in `test/install.test.ts` fakes an older version that shipped an extra file; it failed before the fix and passes now.\n   - A second test checks that a file the user added survives an upgrade. That one already passed, so to make sure it can catch a problem I temporarily made removal delete everything not in the new tree, saw it fail, and restored the code.\n\nI added two notes to `AGENTS.md`: each Python test file has to be listed in the `test` script or it never runs, and how upgrades now remove dropped files. My notes are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":